  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1208 AM CDT Wed Jun 24 2026\n\nAn upper level high will be centered over the northern Chihuahua \nstate in Mexico on Thursday, and then the ridge aloft will become \nelongated from Mexico east across Texas and the Gulf coast Friday \nand Saturday. Associated subsidence will result in minimal rain \nchances for our area, and surface pressure gradient across our area \nwill be enough to maintain breezy south winds each day. Highs \nThursday will be similar, perhaps a degree warmer than today \n(generally from the mid 90s southeast to 102-104 northwest). With a \nslight strengthening of the 850mb thermal ridge, an uptick in highs \nis expected Friday into the weekend. A Heat Advisory may need to be \nissued for portions of the Big Country, mainly north and west of \nAbilene where current forecast highs are 105-107 degrees.    \n\nAn upper high is progged to build north over the lower Mississippi \nValley on Sunday, as a large upper trough moves east over much of \nthe western third of the CONUS. Early next week the upper trough \nwill maintain a presence over the western CONUS while the upper \nhigh, centered approximately over the Illinois/Kentucky border, will\nbecome more expansive. This expansive high will continue to be \nour dominant weather influence, and expect a continuation of hot \nand above normal temperatures with minimal chance of rain.",
